=== CodeGen.java in R1 ===
commit 42d51c474f85a80a4e3592ddd8c3c7c7fc928f47
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Sep 19 02:30:46 2026 +0000

    A top-level mutable variable is read and written inside the transaction on the compiled path

    Rung 3 emitted a bare GETSTATIC/PUTSTATIC on a non-final field, so a variable
    declared at the top level of a component was outside the transaction that
    `atomic do ... end` really does start -- against
    Specification/basic/expressions/atomic.tex:38-42 -- and a write from inside a
    `for` body or a parallel `do ... also` arm was lost outright, at one thread as
    well as at four. Its singleton field now holds a MutableFValue cell and its
    reads and writes route through Transaction.TXRead/TXWrite, the shape
    LocalMutableVar and MutableTaskVarCodeGen in the same file already used; the
    cell's payload is widened to fortress.AnyType.Any so that a variable of arrow
    or String type verifies, the top-level bindings are registered before any
    initializer is generated, and the twenty-two eagerly built debug arguments in
    Transaction.java and BaseTask.java are guarded with the flag they already have,
    because routing accesses through the transaction had turned a working program
    into a StackOverflowError for any value whose type has no asString of its own.

    Gated by compiler_tests/MutableTopLevelVarInLoop and AtomicTopLevelObjectVar,
    both deterministic and both failing at one thread on the tree each guards, and
    by AtomicTopLevelVar under contention. The bound: this is `atomic` in a
    function body or a loop body -- as the trailing expression of a `do ... also`
    arm the generated class does not verify at all, before the repair or after,
    which is ledger row 322. Six ledger rows, three ledger appends and five FACTS
    lines are folded with it; the batch's gate has not been run.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AmiXNpJxQ6TBwec4vJZHDB

